# Netlify rewrites for Echo's web build.
#
# Expo's static export writes a dynamic route as a literal file — thread/[id].html —
# so a real URL like /thread/abc123 matches nothing on disk and 404s. Every shared
# echo, profile and conversation link is a dynamic route, so without these the
# links Echo puts into the world all break.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the browser keeps the real URL, and expo-router reads the
# id from it on the client. A redirect would rewrite the address bar and lose it.
#
# Generated from the export; regenerate when a dynamic route is added.

/chat-details/*    /chat-details/[id].html   200
/chat-media/*    /chat-media/[id].html   200
/comments/*    /comments/[id].html   200
/e/*    /e/[id].html   200
/evolution/*    /evolution/[rootId].html   200
/group/*    /group/[id].html   200
/listing/*    /listing/[id].html   200
/messages/*    /messages/[id].html   200
/office-hours/*    /office-hours/[id].html   200
/remix/*    /remix/[id].html   200
/salon/*    /salon/[slug].html   200
/thread/*    /thread/[id].html   200
/user/*    /user/[id].html   200

# Anything else unknown falls through to Expo's own not-found page.
/*    /+not-found.html   404
